      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the labeled maximum for adults, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release. The extended-release maximum is 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day, depending on the product. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nThe dose may be a typo. These are options I can enter:\n\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum.\n- **1,700 mg PO per day, divided as 850 mg twice daily with meals.** This is a common maintenance dose.\n- **500 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is a typical starting dose, titrated up over weeks.\n\nTell me which dose you want, or give me a different intended dose within the labeled limit. I'll enter it right away. I'll also need to know whether the formulation is immediate-release or extended-release."
      }
